  "aiken_compiler_of_committed_blueprint": "v1.1.23+8949565",
  "blueprint_reproduced": true,
  "blueprint_reproduced_note": "VERIFIED, not assumed. Upstream committed this blueprint with aiken v1.1.23+8949565, which is also the locally installed compiler, so it was rebuilt from the vendored source in a scratch copy and compared: all 27 validator entries reproduce byte-for-byte, preamble included. This is worth stating explicitly because the sibling pin at src/substandards/rwa-token is in the opposite situation -- upstream's committed blueprint there does NOT reproduce from its own source, so that tree deliberately vendors a rebuild and pins both hashes. Here no such exception is needed. The previous core pin (726d757) was corroborated from the other direction: the backend was running a v1.1.23 rebuild of a v1.1.22-committed blueprint and reproduced every validator byte for byte.",
  "backend_resource_copy": "src/programmable-tokens-offchain-java/src/main/resources/plutus.json",
